From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:57:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/36] A new Song has a forward sequence direction: initialize
 TimelineCounter::sequenceDirectionMode

TimelineCounter::sequenceDirectionMode was never initialized; Clip sets it, the Song (the other
TimelineCounter, song automation) never does. A Song made in reused memory could have a reverse or
ping-pong mode. With currentlyPlayingReversed set as well, recording song automation froze with
E445 in AutoParam::homogenizeRegion() (fuzz seed 108).

v1.3.0 (#5094) initializes currentlyPlayingReversed, the other half of the former 0105.

Test (beta-1.3/tests): song_reversed_emu.py.
---
 src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h b/src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h
index ce3663fed..89800cf4f 100644
--- a/src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h
+++ b/src/deluge/model/timeline_counter.h
@@ -52,5 +52,7 @@ public:
 	bool armedForRecording{true};
 
 	bool currentlyPlayingReversed{false};
-	SequenceDirection sequenceDirectionMode;
+	// Clip sets this; the Song, the other TimelineCounter (song automation), never does. Uninitialized, a Song made in
+	// reused memory could have a reverse or ping-pong mode (#5094 initialized currentlyPlayingReversed only)
+	SequenceDirection sequenceDirectionMode{SequenceDirection::FORWARD};
 };
